@meta
id: 20-10
title: The delete history
chapter: 20
type: lesson
skills: register-named
par: 40
minutes: 6
vscode: undo three times, copy, redo three times, paste
open: order.provider.ts

@brief
Every time you delete a line or more, vim files it in a numbered
register. The newest is `"1`; what was in `"1` shifts to `"2`, and so on
down to `"9`, where it falls off. That is nine deletes of history you
did not know you had, and it means "I deleted that a while ago and I
want it back" does not need undo.

Logging is moving out of this provider. Delete all three
`this.logger.debug` lines, top to bottom. Then — the ticket changed
under you — the one in `findOne` has to stay after all. Put it back
exactly where it was, from the history, without retyping it and without
undoing the other two deletes.

@keys
| `"1p` | put the most recent delete |
| `"2p` `"3p` | the one before, and the one before that |
| `"-` | the small-delete register: deletes of less than a line |
| `:reg 123` | see the last three deletes |

@hints
Three deletes, top to bottom: the `findOne` line is the oldest, so it
has been shifted furthest down the history.
--
`/debug` Enter, `dd`, `n` `dd`, `n` `dd`. Now the `findOne` line is in
`"3`.
--
`/tory.find` Enter puts you on the repository call it used to follow.
`"3p`.

@solution
    /debug<Enter> dd n dd n dd  /tory.find<Enter> "3p  :wq<Enter>

As a rule the numbered registers are filled by deletes of a line or
more — `dd`, `dj`, `d}`, `dap`. A smaller delete like `dw` or `di'` goes into
`"-` instead, the small-delete register, so it does not push your line
history around. And nothing you yank ever enters the numbers; yanks go
to `"0`, which is why `"0` is stable.

Between `"0`, `"-` and `"1` to `"9`, vim is keeping eleven things for
you at all times without being asked. `:reg` shows them. Most people
only ever use `"1` and `"2`, but knowing the shelf is there changes how
freely you delete.

@start order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });
    this.logger.debug('findOne', id);

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);
    this.logger.debug('cancel', id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    await this.paymentService.refund(order.id);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }

  public async settle(id: string, total: number) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);
    this.logger.debug('settle', id);

    await this.paymentService.capture(order.id, total);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'SETTLED' },
    });
  }
}

@expected order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });
    this.logger.debug('findOne', id);

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    await this.paymentService.refund(order.id);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }

  public async settle(id: string, total: number) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    await this.paymentService.capture(order.id, total);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'SETTLED' },
    });
  }
}
